    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3124" root="بل" body-key="b">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بُلَالَةٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَلَلٌ</span>, in two places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also The
<i>quantity with which a thing is moistened.</i> (Har
p. 107.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And <i>A remain,</i> or <i>remainder;</i> (T,
and Har ubi suprá;) as also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُلُالَةٌ</span>. (Har ubi
suprá.) You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا فِيهِ بُلَالَةٌ وَلَا عُلَالَةٌ</span> <i>There is
not in it anything remaining.</i> (T, and Har ubi
suprá.)

